A||||17||87FieroGTx||2.8 to 3.4 STROKER???||||5||
Z||000000||87FieroGTx||09-25-2001||11:12 PM|||| Today I went to a shop that just opened in my town. I asked the owner if she had any experince working on Fiero's and she yelled I LOVE FIERO's. <P> So I asked her if she could put a Firebird 3.4 in for me and she asked me why not just stroke the 2.8 to a 3.4. Up till then I thought a 3.1 was the largest you could stroke a 2.8<P> She said she could build me a streetable (250hp) All forged 3.4 stroker for 2k and install it for another 1k<P> So I guess my question is, is this BS or can it be done? <P> If it can be done I may forget the 3800 and Turbo a 3.4  (350hp) for 6k sounds like a good deal to me!||||reg||5
Z||000001||FieroKyle||09-25-2001||11:19 PM||||I want her NUMBER!!!! Damn.... 3k???? I wanted her to do my car, 250 hp? WOW!!! I would love that! Naturally asperated too!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"> of course have her do yours first and tell me how it turns out.||||reg||1
Z||000002||fiero56||09-25-2001||11:31 PM||||longest stroke crank is 3.1, even 3.4 uses 3.1 crank. You need a 3.4 block and 3.1 crank with 3.4 pistons.||||reg||1
Z||000003||GTMike||09-26-2001||01:12 AM||||she might be thnking of the  dubble over head cam 3.4   cause the push rod is only rated at like 180 at the flywheel.  what could you do to make 80 more hp.    i'm hopeing to put forged pistins in  a 3.4 push rod and run a trubo and hope  to get around 250 hp.   if you get a chance ask her what she does to get 250 hp.  i'm intrested<p>[This message has been edited by GTMike (edited 09-26-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||87FieroGTx||09-26-2001||03:54 AM|||| She said they port the heads, hot cam, roller rockers, ported TB/intake, Hi-comp pistons (9:5 maybe a litle high for a turbo) Lucas injectors, Ported exaust man prob a lot I forgot.<P> I will ask more next week when we meet again.<P> Only prob I see with this setup is with the intake and exaust so OPEN the low end torque will suffer without the forced induction.<P> I also wonder if it would pass emitions in NY.<P>the real question i need answereed is is it possible to stroke a 2.8 to 3.4? I found a lot of websites that say its been done but I won't belive it till I talk to soeone who I trust.<P> This is NOT the person I'm talking about but they do sell the 2.8 - 3.4 stroker!<P>       <A HREF="http://www.engine-parts.com/GMV6/gm34da.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.engine-parts.com/GMV6/gm34da.html</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||lou_dias||09-26-2001||09:08 AM||||it needs to both stroked and bored.<P>3.50" is the stock 2.8 and 3.1 bore<BR>3.62" is the stock 3.4 bore<P>2.99" is the stock 2.8 stroke<BR>3.31" is the stroke from 3.1's and 3.4's||||reg||1
Z||000006||Joe Torma||09-26-2001||11:23 AM||||I doubt there is enough metal to bore out the 2.8 block safely.  .062 over?  <P>Get the 3.4 block!<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/simplesig1.gif">  <BR>Did you get your car in my book yet????<BR> <A HREF="http://www.animatedconcepts.com/fierobook.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.animatedconcepts.com/fierobook.htm</A>||||reg||1
Z||000007||lou_dias||09-26-2001||12:27 PM||||A 3.4 has a .122" overbore over a 2.8 (just under an eighth of an inch)<P>I had my original 3.1 stroker bored .060 over.  I think it worked out to 3.275L<BR>Ran it for 50k hard miles before I got rod knock from worn out bearings.<P>Then I got a used 95 Camaro 3.4 with 17k on it and threw a rod through the block in under 100 miles...<P>Who was is that was going to de-stroke a 3.4 and go really high compression to favor HP?||||reg||1
Z||000008||LAMBO||09-26-2001||01:12 PM|||| <A HREF="http://www.engine-parts.com/GMV6/gm34da.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.engine-parts.com/GMV6/gm34da.html</A> <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000009||fierobear||09-26-2001||01:17 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Joe Torma:<BR><B>I doubt there is enough metal to bore out the 2.8 block safely.  .062 over?  <P>Get the 3.4 block!<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>From what I'm told, you can't bore the 2.8 to 3.4 safely. Not enough metal. The 3.4 has a different internal setup from the factory. A 2.8 wouldn't have enough stuff left after you bore it out that big.||||reg||1
Z||000010||Formula||09-26-2001||01:18 PM||||My 3.1 Camaro engine was bored 60 over with the 3.1 crank... I thought that was a 3.2?<P>apparantly mine was dynoed at 270 hp at 7000 rpms before I bought it (motor) so Im sure it can be done.  I still can't get it to run all the way up to 7k right with the igniton coil being a OEM style one though.  It still can walk a 260 hp 2001 Mustang GT fairl easy.<P>I'd say go for it!!<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Formulasigs.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000011||MinnGreenGT||09-26-2001||01:29 PM||||Do you have anything else done to your 3200 stroker?  I'm running a very similiar setup, but I'm generous in estimating 200hp... where'd you get the other 70 from? (I want 'em <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">)<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/grngtsig3.jpg">     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fullstaff.gif">   <BR>Medium Metallic Green 87 GT<BR>3.1L High Output<BR>4 Spd OD Tranny<BR>Open (read: Loud) Exhaust<BR>and More!<BR>-Rob Bartlett||||reg||1
Z||000012||Raydar||09-26-2001||02:27 PM||||There's a guy in our club that has a 3.4 that used to be a 2.8. It *can* be done. I believe he did the work himself.<BR>ARI hand picks the blocks and tests them to make sure the casting will be thick enough. <P>No "fudge factor", though. <BR>I'd also hate to overheat one.<P><BR><P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000013||lou_dias||09-26-2001||03:26 PM||||Take my advice.  If you want to save money, don't worry about going all the way to a 3.4 right off the bat.  go .030 over or whatever your machinist bored it to to get the cylinders straight again and then you won't have to worry about another block when it's time to rebuild again, just bore again ... and again.  If you're lucky, you won't have a 3.4 until your car hit 300k miles.  Spend your money on the real important stuff like porting and a hot cam.  The difference between a 3.1 and a 3.4 is 13-16 cubic inches, but that doesn't equal 13-16 horses if your engine can flow enough fuel and air.||||reg||1
Z||000014||Formula||09-26-2001||04:00 PM||||I still havent got the build sheets on it but, it has a huge cam, everything inside is forged.  He has over $3000 in receipts on the motor.  I know that the heads were ported, polished, shaved.  The block was C&Ced, bored 60 over, stroked.  it was balanced and blue printed.  different rocker arms then stock (they looked bigger).  it has a windage tray and a hig volume oil pump.  the intake manifold was ported and polished.  It has a holley 390 carb that cant seem to give it enough gas straight out of the box.  <P>if he cant find the build sheets then I'll get it dynoed when I get it to run perfect.||||reg||1
Z||000015||Formula||09-26-2001||04:01 PM||||it was making 270 with open headers (big). so I doubt that I'll get that with the fiero manifolds.||||reg||1
Z||000016||87FieroGTx||09-26-2001||10:57 PM|||| Would the walls be thick enough for a turbo?||||reg||5
Z||000017||lou_dias||09-27-2001||09:56 AM||||I think this "get a 3.4 block, a 2.8 one isn't reliable" is just marketing crap.<P>For the engineers to "beef up" the block, they would have to either use different material or change the whole block because the thinnest point of the walls is between the cylinders on the same bank.  And to thinken that, they would have to change the cylinder spacing ... and crank ... and BLOCK ... and HEADS ... and EVERYTHING else.<P>What might make a 2.8 block unreliable is age/stress cracks and the fact that if it's a pre 87 block, is probably doesn't have the oiling update which can be done anyway.<P>I threw a rod right through a "real" 3.4 block so you ain't getting any benefits there.  Ask Ed at the Fiero Factory.  He saw my block in April of 2000.  My only mod to the engine was putting in a POS crane 2030 cam.||||reg||1
